# Bash 3.2 parse verification: tests/fm-pi-watch-extension.test.sh

Change under test: 3587605 (comment rewording only, 3 lines, all // comments inside JS heredoc bodies)
Base: f49ebc4

## 1. Minimal reproduction of the defect mechanism (bash 3.2.57)
```
$ cat minimal.sh
# Minimal reproduction of the Bash 3.2 defect: an apostrophe inside a comment
# in a $( ... <<'EOF' ... EOF ) heredoc body is parsed as shell code.
out=$(node --input-type=module 2>&1 <<'EOF'
// the branch's model turn
console.log("hi");
EOF
)
printf '%s\n' "$out"

$ docker run --rm -v /w bash:3.2 -c "bash -n /w/minimal.sh"
/w/minimal.sh: line 8: unexpected EOF while looking for matching `''
/w/minimal.sh: line 9: syntax error: unexpected end of file
exit=2
```

